      "id": "b011",
      "chapter": "s2",
      "kind": "narration",
      "display": {
        "en": "The Earth also travels around the Sun. One trip takes one year, or about three hundred and sixty-five days. Because of the tilt, the same part of the Earth leans toward the Sun for part of the trip and leans away for another part."
      },
