    {
      "id": "b014",
      "chapter": "s3",
      "kind": "narration",
      "display": {
        "en": "When your half of the Earth leans toward the Sun, sunlight hits the ground more directly. The days are longer, and the land warms up. That is summer. When your half leans away, the sunlight comes in at a low angle and spreads out. The days are shorter, and it gets cold. That is winter."
      },
      "spoken": {
        "en": "When your half of the Earth leans toward the Sun, sunlight hits the ground more directly. The days are longer, and the land warms up. That is summer. When your half leans away, the sunlight comes in at a low angle and spreads out. The days are shorter, and it gets cold. That is winter."
      },
